==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From [[w:James Alfred Van Allen|James Alfred Van Allen]], US [[physicist]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[van|Van]] [[Allen]] [[radiation belt]]}}

# {{context|astronomy|physics}} Either of two [[torus]]-shaped areas of high-energy [[charge]]d [[particle]]s which partly [[surround]] [[Earth]], trapped by its [[magnetic field]]. The areas are characterised by intense [[radiation]]. When the belts "overload", particles strike the upper atmosphere and [[fluoresce]], causing the [[polar]] [[aurora]].

